# Cloudflare Pages merges every block whose pattern matches a request, and joins
# repeated header values with a comma. So the broad rule below also reaches
# /_astro/*, and two Cache-Control values would contradict each other
# ("immutable, must-revalidate"). The asset block detaches the inherited value
# with the documented `!` syntax before declaring its own.

# Everything, HTML included: revalidate on every request so a deploy is visible
# immediately, plus the security headers that apply to the whole site.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# Build assets carry a content hash in the file name: a new build produces a new
# URL, so these can be cached for a year and never revalidated.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
